        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{7}{(2x+1)^2}$",
          "worked": "Let $u=3x-2$ and $v=2x+1$, so $u'=3$ and $v'=2$.\n$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac{u'v-uv'}{v^2}\\\\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac{3(2x+1)-2(3x-2)}{(2x+1)^2}\\\\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac{6x+3-6x+4}{(2x+1)^2}\\\\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac7{(2x+1)^2}\\end{aligned}$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
